# SFT execution status v0.83

2026-09-13. The local control-only real-import preparation is complete. This
adds no new roadmap gate and does not execute a checkpoint import. Gate 5
remains incomplete. The successful v0.2 tiny Linux CPU qualification and both
CI runs are preserved; they were not rerun.

## What was completed

A pure metadata contract now binds the exact frozen import plan and successful
qualification verification. Its deterministic preparer verifies twelve fixed
control/source files (260,864 bytes per pass) and evaluates only the newly
written standard-library contract module. Two sequential zero-network
preparation passes produced identical results. The saved contract is
`configs/lumi-4b-sft-checkpoint-host-contract-v0.1.json`.

The first 19 synthetic contract tests were expanded with nine file-binding and
preparer tests: 28 tests pass on local Python 3.13.7. Their fixture inputs are
generated control JSON, not model or dataset payloads. The final test run denied
network, subprocess, native-library loading and ML imports. New Python files
also passed syntax and 100-column checks. No new Linux-native run or Ruff result
is claimed.

The checks cover budget arithmetic, boolean/invalid limits, omitted conversion
and package reads, missing config/control write reserves, insufficient disk/RAM,
wrong owner/mode requirements, altered bindings and attempts to turn a planning
document into execution permission. Errors expose fixed codes only.

Independent source review found no blocker for this inert scope. The proposed
envelope checker is deliberately not a full-size sufficiency proof: the real
package finalizer traverses payload/tokenizer content three times and also
reads/writes receipt and manifest controls. The successor must derive and test
that complete budget before admission; the current sufficiency flag is false.

## Concrete full-size requirements

The frozen plan declares 48,839,117,190 checkpoint bytes and 4,648,253 tokenizer
bytes. Two full audits total 97,687,530,886 logical source bytes. That is not the
whole read budget: DCP model reads, HF output reads and packaging reads are
additional. The DCP cap already includes the first full checkpoint audit, so
only one additional checkpoint audit belongs in the coordinator formula.

Planning RAM is at least 68,719,476,736 bytes (64 GiB). Private output writes
remain capped at 8,415,205,181 bytes. The 57,258,970,624-byte staging figure covers
checkpoint, tokenizer and output; the selected host must additionally reserve
space for accepted software, scratch and other explicitly accounted storage.
These are planning figures, not actual host admission or performance estimates.

The frozen checkpoint reader requires UID/GID 10001 in the planned worker,
directories 0700 and files 0600. Read-only mount flags are separate from those
permission bits. Existing files must not be changed to root-owned/0400 as a
shortcut. Proposed `/inputs/checkpoint`, `/inputs/tokenizer` and `/outputs`
targets are namespace layout requirements, not acquired host paths. Other
writable aliases/writers must be excluded; a read-only bind alone is not an
immutability proof. The original tokenizer subdirectory semantics stay intact.

The tiny qualification's 4 GiB memory, 90-second guard and 512 MiB scratch are
not full-size admission limits. They remain unchanged.

## Exact remaining work

1. Implement and test the separately versioned real-input mount/full-size runner
   adapter. The existing `run_import` remains closed with `host_guard_not_bound`.
2. Bind a dedicated host, accepted runtime/source closure, input backing-store
   strategy and explicitly approved full-size read/write/time/resource envelope.
   Observe the host/mount/control readbacks before acquiring or importing data.
3. Execute the separately authorized real checkpoint import, then complete the
   already documented GPU-worker, private-data and CUDA/smoke prerequisites
   before SFT. This preparation does not skip any of them.

No host was selected or provisioned. No network, S3, GPU, inference, training,
real payload reads, source mutation, registry change, commit or push occurred.
The new preparation files are local only. GPU is not needed for the current
control-code work; do not turn it on for this step.

Report: `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-checkpoint-host-preparation-v0.1.json`.
Structural verification: matching `host-preparation-verification-v0.1.json`.
